  "_comment": "Cross-engine guard for an Apply EDL render's clipKey (A1b review rounds): a selector on the render's edl wire, and one on the Edit Plan to Camera Switch wire. Row k of an each wire is row k of what its selector picks, never row k of the plan. A wire that hands on ONE value (Selected, item, item:N, all) names the clip it picks, as both input resolvers pick it (decided 2026-10-05); such a render runs once (expectedRows null). Selected (outputMode last) is the plan's own output, its FIRST clip. `direct` cases also check the key is the span of the EDL the render receives. The backend test (apply-edl-clip-key.test.ts) and the editor test of the same name read this file. `dropped` (optional) lists the plan clips the person dropped in review (the TA16 holes: \"\" at each in the plan list); the harnesses apply it as the plan's editedEdl.",
